  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Algebra 2 is really the study of <em>functions</em> as objects you can combine, invert and transform. Fluency with notation, domain and range underpins every later chapter.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 1.1 — Function",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A <strong>function</strong> assigns to each input exactly one output. We write \\( y=f(x) \\); the set of allowed inputs is the <strong>domain</strong> and the set of resulting outputs is the <strong>range</strong>.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Composition",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (f\\circ g)(x)=f\\big(g(x)\\big) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Inverse",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "swap \\( x \\) and \\( y \\), then solve for \\( y \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Domain rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "no division by 0; no even root of a negative",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Inverse check",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f\\big(f^{-1}(x)\\big)=x \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Given \\( f(x)=2x+1 \\) and \\( g(x)=x^{2} \\), find \\( f\\big(g(2)\\big) \\).</p><p>Work inside-out: \\( g(2)=4 \\), then \\( f(4)=2(4)+1 \\):</p>\\[ f\\big(g(2)\\big)=9. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the inverse of \\( f(x)=2x-6 \\).</p><p>Write \\( y=2x-6 \\), swap and solve: \\( x=2y-6 \\Rightarrow y=\\tfrac{x+6}{2} \\):</p>\\[ f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+6}{2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "If \\(f(x)=x^2-1\\) and \\(g(x)=\\sqrt{x+2}\\), find (a) \\(f(g(3))\\), (b) the domain of \\(g\\circ f\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "(a) \\(g(3)=\\sqrt5\\); \\(f(\\sqrt5)=5-1=4\\). (b) \\(g(f(x))=\\sqrt{x^2-1+2}=\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\); always real, domain: all reals.",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
